@4835. (Swab) feared that the Lord would drive him out from that dominion; on which account, as a means of exercising command, he assumed the doctrine of charity, and acknowledged the Lord as the only God; thus believing that as he made one with the others who were around me, dominion would be granted to him.

@4839[end]. They concluded that they would have dominion, and when it was said that the last were first, they concluded that they would sit in the last place while they were commanding...

